# Documentation Usage Rules

  - Read relevant documentation before proposing architectural changes.
  - Use only pages accessible to the current user or authorized tools.
  - Do not assume that a URL has been read merely because it is listed here.
  - Verify that retrieved documentation is current and relevant.
  - Prefer the applicable, current project specification when
    documenting expected system behavior.
  - If documentation conflicts with existing code or an approved
    decision, report the conflict rather than silently choosing.
  - Do not copy entire pages into change specifications.
  - Summarize only the requirements and decisions relevant to the change.
  - Record material assumptions and unresolved documentation gaps.
